TechInsights has published an <a href="https://www.techinsights.com/blog/apple-iphone-18-pro-max-teardown">iPhone 18 Pro Max teardown</a> that confirms the U.S. version of the device is equipped with Qualcomm's Snapdragon X80 modem.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/deep-black-iphone-18-pro.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063303" /><br/>
The device's <a href="https://x.com/itspdfu/status/2100954259999109388">modem firmware</a> had already pointed towards the Snapdragon X80 modem.<br/>
<br/>
The smaller iPhone 18 Pro and the iPhone Duo use Apple's custom-designed C2 modem worldwide, and the iPhone 18 Pro Max uses the C2 modem in every other country, so the U.S. version of the iPhone 18 Pro Max having a Qualcomm modem <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/12/iphone-18-pro-max-us-model-difference/">is unique</a>.<br/>
<br/>
iPhone 17 Pro and iPhone 17 Pro Max models <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/19/iphone-17-pro-max-qualcomm-snapdragon-x80/">have the same Snapdragon X80 modem</a> worldwide, although TechInsights noted that the U.S. version of the iPhone 18 Pro Max has a newly-identified mmWave 5G antenna module from Apple.<br/>
<br/>
We will have to wait for C2 vs. Snapdragon X80 performance tests.<br/>
<br/>
Apple has yet to explain why only the U.S. version of the iPhone 18 Pro Max still has a Qualcomm modem, so we can only speculate for now. In 2023, Qualcomm <a href="https://investor.qualcomm.com/news-events/press-releases/news-details/2023/Qualcomm-Announces-Agreement-with-Apple-for-Chip-Supply-09-11-2023/default.aspx">announced</a> that it would supply Apple with smartphone modems through 2026, so perhaps Apple is ensuring that it complies with its contractual obligations in a minimal way.<br/>
<br/>
